0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.18674817323096113,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.18513803204520732,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.030335704047256027,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":49.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.3424,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Atlas Energy Solutions Inc. produces proppants and provides logistics and distributed power solutions in the Permian Basin of West Texas and New Mexico. It operates through two segments: Sand and Logistics, and Power. The Sand and Logistics segment operates fourteen proppant production facilities, including large-scale in-basin plants and a distributed mining network. This segment sells products and services primarily to oil and natural gas exploration and production companies, hydraulic fracturing services, and oilfield services companies; and produces locally sourced proppants, such as 40/70-mesh and 100-mesh sand, as well as both dry and damp sand options. It also offers a differentiated logistics platform featuring a fleet of fit-for-purpose trucks, trailers, wellsite equipment, and a 42-mile Dune Express conveyor system for proppant delivery. The Power segment provides distributed power solutions through a fleet of natural gas-powered reciprocating generators designed for heavy-duty, mission-critical applications, primarily supporting oil and gas production and artificial lift operations. The company also offers transportation, storage, contract labor, and distributes power rentals to the oil and gas industry. Atlas Energy Solutions Inc. formerly known as New Atlas HoldCo. Inc. Atlas Energy Solutions Inc. was founded in 2017 and is headquartered in Austin, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John G. Turner | President, CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $725K ranks in the below the sector median among Energy peers, improving at 34%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $22K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Atlas Energy Solutions Inc. is a small-cap energy business with a $678M market cap on $1.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +34% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 22% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $31M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin -0.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 18.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 34% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"